  "id": "zero_sum.zero_sum_payoff_negation",
  "title": "Payoff Negation in Zero-Sum Games",
  "kind": "lemma",
  "status": "formalized",
  "href": "zero_sum/zero_sum_zero_sum_payoff_negation.html",
  "body_html": "<h1>Payoff Negation in Zero-Sum Games</h1>\n<p>If $G$ is zero-sum, then at every profile $\\sigma$ the payoff of either player\ndetermines the other:</p>\n<p>$$u_1(\\sigma) = -u_0(\\sigma), \\qquad u_0(\\sigma) = -u_1(\\sigma).$$</p>\n<p>This is the algebraic reduction that lets later value and optimality statements\ntrack only the row player's payoff.</p>",
